Found by the k390 worker (2026-11-06), not fixed there. (1) lib/OCP/Keys.pm update_key (~:287) puts a PIN2 layer on private without checking pin2: an undefined PIN2 derives the layer from an empty password, and it would put a PIN2 layer on an automation key. Nothing in lib/ or bin/ calls update_key today. (2) The add_key POD (~:797) says "Required params: ... pin2"; pin2 is optional (automation keys). Done = update_key refuses a missing pin2 for a non-automation key and never adds a PIN2 layer to an automation key (or update_key goes, since nothing calls it), and the POD says pin2 is optional. Lane: ocp-secrets-worker.

2026-11-26 05:31 Done: kept update_key and fixed it rather than removing it -- deprecate_key is built on it (t/05-keys.t pins deprecate_key), so removing it means rewriting deprecate_key and the two croak messages that point at it. A new private half is now layered by the key's purpose, as add_key does: automation = age only, pin2 ignored; every other key = age + PIN2, croaking 'update_key: PIN2 required ...' before anything is written when pin2 is undef/empty ('0' is a PIN2, k390). POD: update_key documented; add_key says name/type/private required, pin2 optional (and what each layering means). Repro: new t/411-update-key-pin2.t red against HEAD (empty PIN2 accepted and the admin key re-layered with an empty password; the script then died reading it with the old PIN2), green after. Verified in the image: t/411, t/05-keys.t pass.
